WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:05.799
Hey youtubers it's Charlie, and my friends
at Geek and Sundry are making this cool new

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:10.020
Gae Bolg from Final Fantasy Realm Reborn in
real life, so I wanted to do another bonus

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.800
video talking about the Lore of the Game and
some of the other legendary weapons and put

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.179
it into perspective with the rest of the Final
Fantasy Series.

00:00:18.179 --> 00:00:22.710
So in the episode they talk a little about
why the Gae Bolg is so much cooler than 99

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:27.390
Percent of all the other weapons. It's Legendary,
anyone who's played WoW or really any MMO

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:32.029
for that matter knows that Legendary Items
appear like once or twice on a server with

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:36.940
a few exceptions. There are craftable Legendaries,
just weapons that start out being cool and

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:43.070
allow you to reforge with other rare boss
drops till eventually you have your Legendary.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:47.710
I think in WoW my guild had to grind Firelands
on Heroic for a month just to get our Boomkin

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.260
his Dragonwrath staff. The fun kind of wore
off after the first few weeks, but look how

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:52.780
shiny!

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:58.070
In Realm Reborn the Gae Bolg is one of 9 Relic
Weapons that you obtain after an epic boss

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:02.090
grind and a bunch of other mission completions.
The start quest is actually titled "A Relic

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:07.060
Reborn". The weapons are all specific to each
Job. They are, in no particular order:

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.390
The Artemis Bow for the Bard

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.400
The Bravura for the Warrior

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.900
The Curtana and Holy Shield for the Paladin

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.450
The Gae Bolg for the Dragoon

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.790
The Omnilex for the Scholar

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.330
The Sphairai for the Monk

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.790
The Stardust Rod for the Mage

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:25.150
The Veil of Wiyu for the Summoner

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.150
and The Thyrus for the White Mage

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:32.770
You could write a book for the steps needed
to obtain all these relic weapons, so generally

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:39.360
once you get one, you have one of the best
weapons in the game. Usually it takes a new

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:45.070
expansion before everything gets nerfed and
there's a new precious to grind for.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:49.190
In their new video Nika actually talked to
one of the GMs from Square Enix about Dragoons

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:54.290
specifically just because they forged a Gae
Bolg in real life. Dragoons are historically

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:59.220
famous for fighting Dragons, but they've been
featured in all of the Final Fantasy Games

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:06.150
since Final Fantasy 2. Sometimes it's just
as reference and not as a playable character.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:11.930
Final Fantasy 4 on the Super Nintendo was
my introduction to Dragoons and the Series

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:16.990
in General. In that game Kain was the only
Dragoon and he was more of a foil for you

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:22.540
as the protagonist. In each iteration of the
game the Gae Bolg is the signature weapon.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.870
It looks like a pike just because they needed
to be able to fight dragons without having

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:31.140
to get in close like you would with a traditional
sword. So I applaud the creators of all the

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:36.980
different games for keeping character traits
consistent across 30 plus years of a game

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.950
franchise. That's better continuity than the
X-Men Movie Franchise.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:47.170
Realm Reborn incorporates a lot of the lore
of the Dragoons built up since the beginning

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:50.980
of the franchise. So if you've played a lot
of different versions of the game your character

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:57.819
traits and skills will look really familiar.
It also pays homage to a lot of Dragoon characters

00:02:57.819 --> 00:03:01.879
you encounter having the surname Highwind
just because across the franchise they've

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:05.360
kept it a thing that all of the dragoons flow
from Kain Highwind and his family. They built

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:11.069
a lot of that lore into the old Final Fantasy
2 game back in the 80s. So JRPGs aren't just

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:13.410
cool now, they've always been that cool.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:18.670
That's why you see a lot of story teams created
when big western games like Halo or other

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.790
Western RPGs are in development. People in
America learned from Japanese game makers

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:27.400
how important story are lore was and started
to integrate it into new games. That's why

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.980
the best games always have the best stories.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:36.980
If you look at the Gae Bolg Nika built yes
she's not a giant, but the scale is 1 to 1.

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:42.870
So if you were using a polearm on Game of
Thrones or any other medieval series. It would

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:47.629
be the same size. They got a person to test
it out, he's part of the Armored Combat League.

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:52.269
They're like a sports league that LARPS and
uses real life armor and weapons to do tourney

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:57.150
sports. So all the stuff you see them using
you would have also seen on the battlefield

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:57.519
in the middle ages.

00:03:57.519 --> 00:04:01.250
They got to stab a lot of stuff and even tried
to replicate the Dragoon jump attack. You

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:05.530
have to remember real life physics kind of
sucks, just because you're carrying like an

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.620
extra hundred pounds of weight. So it would
be like strapping cinder blocks to your feet

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.340
and trying to slam dunk a basketball. If you
can do that, you're probably making millions

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.019
of dollars in the NBA right now.

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:21.440
I'd say my other favorite class to play in
Final Fantasy games is Black Mage, yes they're

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.250
super cool to watch, but from a practical
standpoint if you can learn to deal with being

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:32.600
a squishy cloth wearer, you get way more powerful
attacks. So you're one of the best DPS classes.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.210
Unless you're fighting someone with high magic
resist. Then yes, you're just squishy. Usually

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.790
it's a lot easier to learn melee classes first
just because it's a lot of hack and slash.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.110
But I think Mages are way more useful later
in the game.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:47.830
The issue you run into with MMOs in general
is class tuning, so as you start maxing out

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:52.300
your gear, all classes start to become equally
useful in raid.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:59.300
So Realm Reborn is basically Final Fantasy
14 and even though they released Lightning

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:10.660
Returns recently, Final Fantasy 15 has been
in development since before 2006. They even

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:18.000
showed footage of it at E3 in 2006. The reason
it takes so long to release a new numbered

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.400
sequel to the franchise is because they change
everything about the game so much with each

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.250
new iteration.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:31.250
And remember what games looked like in 2006
versus right now. They've had to redesign

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:39.870
everything several times. There isn't any
official release date other than 2015 fingers

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:46.050
crossed. In keeping with recent tradition,
the game jumps to a much more modern looking

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:51.120
time, like the difference between Final Fantasy
8 and Final Fantasy 9, one is super techy

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.860
and the other is super steam punky.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:58.669
The last update we got from Square Enix was
in February, and they said it was really far

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:02.600
into development, that's kind of vague, so
I'm expecting it to drop around November or

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:09.600
December 2015 unless we get to E3 next year
and they have nothing. Games take way longer

00:06:11.039 --> 00:06:14.930
to make than movies, so don't be surprised
if it takes even longer to finish.

